   "source": [
    "## 4. Missing data — most appropriate treatment method per column, with justification"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7a3a10ab",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Inspect how much is missing per column first\n",
    "missing_summary = df.isnull().sum().sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "missing_pct = (df.isnull().mean() * 100).round(2)\n",
    "pd.DataFrame({'missing_count': missing_summary, 'missing_%': missing_pct}).sort_values('missing_%', ascending=False)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d0152f45",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Justification (edit/adjust after you inspect your own missing_summary output):**\n",
    "\n",
    "| Column | Recommended treatment | Why |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Time | Fill with a placeholder (e.g. `\"Unknown\"`) or drop the column if analysis doesn't need it | Time of day is not central to most questions in this exercise and often has heavy missingness in older records |\n",
    "| Operator | Mode imputation or `\"Unknown\"` placeholder | Categorical; a single missing operator has minimal effect on aggregate stats |\n",
    "| Flight # | Fill with `\"Unknown\"` / drop | Mostly an identifier, not used for analysis in this exercise |\n",
    "| Route | Fill with `\"Unknown\"` | Free-text field, hard to impute meaningfully; not required for any question here |\n",
    "| Type | Mode imputation or `\"Unknown\"` | Categorical aircraft type; mode is a reasonable stand-in |\n",
    "| Registration | Drop rows or fill `\"Unknown\"` | Unique identifier per aircraft — imputing a value would be misleading, so leave as missing/placeholder |\n",
    "| cn/In | Fill with `\"Unknown\"` | Construction/serial number, not used in this exercise |\n",
    "| Aboard | Median imputation | Numeric; median is robust to the outliers common in crash data (some flights carried very few, others hundreds) |\n",
    "| Fatalities | Median imputation, or drop rows if used as the key outcome variable | Numeric outcome variable — since several questions rely directly on Fatalities, dropping rows with missing Fatalities is safer than guessing a value |\n",
    "| Ground | Fill with 0 | A blank usually means no fatalities on the ground (not \"unknown\"), so 0 is a defensible default |\n",
    "| Summary | Fill with `\"No summary available\"` | Free-text description, not used numerically |\n",
    "\n",
    "General rule applied: numeric columns central to the analysis (Fatalities, Aboard) → median imputation or row drop; identifier/free-text columns → `\"Unknown\"` placeholder or left as-is since they aren't used downstream."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3c08c6a6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Example of applying the treatments above (adjust to match your own column names/casing)\n",
    "df['Fatalities'] = df['Fatalities'].fillna(df['Fatalities'].median())\n",
    "df['Aboard'] = df['Aboard'].fillna(df['Aboard'].median())\n",
    "df['Ground'] = df['Ground'].fillna(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "text_cols = ['Time', 'Operator', 'Flight #', 'Route', 'Type', 'Registration', 'cn/In', 'Summary']\n",
    "for c in text_cols:\n",
    "    if c in df.columns:\n",
    "        df[c] = df[c].fillna('Unknown')\n",
    "\n",
    "df.isnull().sum()\n"
   ]
  }
